# Backend best practices (ark-shop-back)

Apply these skills when editing this codebase:

| Skill | Focus |
|-------|--------|
| `nestjs-clean-typescript` | Typed NestJS modules, naming, small functions |
| `prisma` | Schema indexes, `select`/`include`, transactions |
| `jwt-security` | Minimal JWT payload (`sub`, `role`, `jti`), hashed refresh tokens, `iss`/`aud` |
| `supabase-postgres-best-practices` | Composite indexes, query patterns |
| `postgresql-code-review` | SQL/migration review |
| `test-driven-development` | Tests before behavior changes |
| `systematic-debugging` | Reproduce before fixing |
| `verification-before-completion` | Run `npm run lint` and `npm run test` |
| `docker-compose-orchestration` | Compose healthchecks, test stack |
| `github-actions-docs` | CI workflow changes |
| `sentry` | No PII in events; scrub auth headers |

## Project-specific rules

- Never put email or passwords in JWT payloads.
- Use `select` on Prisma reads; avoid returning `password` fields.
- Refresh tokens: store SHA-256 hash only; rotate on refresh.
- Keys module: never log or expose plaintext `keyData`.
- Payment webhooks: verify signatures using raw body middleware.
- After `prisma/schema.prisma` changes: `npm run prisma:migrate` and `npm run prisma:generate`.
